      "content": "You mentioned the `history` vector might be an issue. I see that now—we are pushing packet sizes into it every single time `processBuffer` is called, and we aren't currently clearing it out. \n\nBut even if we fix the vector, the memory exhaustion is still happening quite aggressively in some test runs. Beyond just forgetting to clear a container, what are some of the more subtle or \"sneaky\" ways memory gets lost in C++ that might not look like a blatant missing `delete`? I'm trying to understand the logic of how these small leaks actually \"hide\" from a developer during a normal inspection.",
